        drivingExperience: "The 1.8 TFSI (CABA) with 120hp provides a very bizarre driving experience from the factory. Because it is an artificially software-restricted version of the 160hp engine, it spools instantly and feels incredibly punchy off the line, delivering its 230Nm torque beautifully. However, the moment you pass 4000 RPM, the ECU violently cuts boost, and the engine feels like it runs completely out of breath, flatlining all the way to the redline. It is quiet, highly refined, and very smooth, but it desperately begs to be tuned to unleash its true potential.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The CABA is a brilliant tuning canvas completely ruined by VAG's cost-cutting on internal components. From the factory, it is a ticking time bomb. The original timing chain tensioner WILL fail and destroy the engine, and the microscopic piston oil rings WILL clog and cause the engine to burn massive amounts of oil. If you are buying one, you MUST have physical proof that the timing chain and tensioner have been updated to the latest revision. If the car burns oil, the only fix is a €3000 engine rebuild. If those two flaws are fixed, and you flash it to Stage 1, it becomes a phenomenal, highly reliable 210hp engine.",
        repairCostEstimate: "$800 - $2000 / year (Dependent on timing chain / oil ring status)",
